 "type": "exciter",
 "summary": "Harmonic exciter: high-passes the input, drives it through a soft shaper, high-passes again and adds it back to the dry signal. For brightness and presence on drums, vocals and the mix.",
 "category": "Distortion",
 "tags": [
  "exciter",
  "bright"
 ],
 "use_for": "Add presence and sparkle by blending high-passed, shaped harmonics back in.",
 "quirks": [
  "Adds to the dry signal, so it gets louder as Amount rises (+7.2 dB on noise at the defaults).",
  "Its filter corners are one-pole coefficients; the texts (and these Hz) are its own estimate at 44.1 kHz and move with the sample rate.",
  "Its own texts for the corners divide by the engine's sample rate, which a native has only once the engine has run (before, every corner reads \"1 Hz\"): the corners read through their mappings, its 44.1 kHz estimate.",
  "Stereo in and out."
 ],
